    "done_when": "The currency report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s22-coord/review-dies-currency/report.md, items (3a) and (3b), is the brief. (3a): the fixture dates the two writes apart. The assertion names the later timestamp rather than max() of the returned fields, and the grace is driven from a stream offset that falls between the two writes, so an earlier-write regression changes the stop decision. The named negative control (swap max for min in review_delivered) reddens that assertion. (3b): at reckon/crew/recovery.py:680-682, the manifest_status_is_template operand can never be true when status equals complete. Either remove it, with the reason in the fragment, or reorder the check so a template status is refused before the equality test; in that case add a case in the same test file that feeds a template status and asserts the stop does not fire. Change nothing else in recovery.py. The gate is tests/test_a_delivered_review_ends_its_turn.py and tests/test_crew_recovery.py, plus every test file whose name contains review_delivered or delivered_review, run with -n 8 at base and at head. Both suite arms are recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder; each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. The head arm adds no failure id. Basetemps go under /tmp in a directory named for this run; delete everything created there before status complete, printing what is deleted and listing it in artifacts. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/a-review-dies-where-nobody-is-looking/delivered-review-findings.html records both changes. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete.",
